# Nothing is left sounding (NoteRegistry.flushEvents): a stop sends MIDI Stop, then a note-off for each note sounding,
# by (channel, note), then All Notes Off (CC 123) on each channel that had one (sent from the next ms: the tick sends
# everything); a mute silences the voice's channel, a channel change the old one; the arranger's ending stops on
# its tick. A template switch does not flush (as Transport.swift): what the old piece queued still goes out at its
# own ticks. Tick 0 sounds 100 ms after PLAY is seen (the press's first ms); bar N is tick N x 3840. The dumps go
# to app/build/scenarios/stop_flush/.
#
# the flush's order: the Full ensemble (96 BPM) on its own seed (the boot's project has a fresh one) stopped at tick
# 1505, the bass (channel 3, 2 on the wire) and the pad's chord (channel 4, 3) sounding
rt load full
dumpmidi app/build/scenarios/stop_flush/stop.txt
tap PLAY
wait 1000
tap PLAY
dumpis 1 B3 7B 00
dumpis 2 B2 7B 00
dumpis 3 83 48 00
dumpis 4 83 45 00
dumpis 5 83 40 00
dumpis 6 82 2D 00
dumpis 7 FC 00 00
dumpcount B0 7B 00
expect dumpcount 0
expect sounding 0
#
# Ambient drift (72 BPM, a bar 3333 ms): its drone holds E3 (52, 0x34) and A3 (57, 0x39) on channel 1 (0 on the
# wire), struck every 8 bars for 8 bars
rt load ambient
# stop in bar 20 (the drone struck on bar 16)
tap PLAY
wait 66800
expect playing 1
expect tick 76929
expect sounding0 2
out
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
expect_out USB FC 00 00
expect_out USB 80 34 00
expect_out USB 80 39 00
expect_out USB B0 7B 00
expect sounding 0
expect queued 0
# mute in bar 4 (the drone struck on bar 0): its channel silenced at once; nothing of it on bars 8 to 15; unmuted
# in bar 13, it is struck again on bar 16
tap PLAY
wait 13400
expect tick 15412
expect sounding0 2
out
rt mute drone 1
wait 1
expect_out USB 80 34 00
expect_out USB 80 39 00
expect_out USB B0 7B 00
expect sounding0 0
wait 30000
expect tick 49973
expect sounding0 0
rt mute drone 0
wait 20000
expect tick 73013
expect sounding0 2
# a template switch in bar 20 (tick 78773): on the next bar line (bar 21, tick 80640) the Full ensemble takes over
# with its tempo (96 BPM); the drone (struck on bar 16, not in the new piece) is not silenced there, and muting it
# then (no channel of its own any more) leaves its queued offs alone: they go out on bar 24's line (92160)
wait 5000
expect tick 78773
dumpmidi app/build/scenarios/stop_flush/switch.txt
rt load full
wait 1000
expect tempo_tick -1
wait 1000
expect tick 81223
expect tempo_tick 80640
expect tick_rate 1536
expect bpm 96
expect sounding0.52 1
expect sounding0.57 1
rt mute drone 1
expect sounding0.52 1
wait 7600
expect tick 92897
dumpcount 80 34 00 92160
expect dumpcount 1
dumpcount 80 39 00 92160
expect dumpcount 1
dumpcount B0 7B 00
expect dumpcount 0
expect sounding0.52 0
expect sounding0.57 0
expect playing 1
tap PLAY
# a channel change in bar 4: the drone's old channel silenced at once, its next notes (bar 8) on the new one
rt load ambient
tap PLAY
wait 13400
expect sounding0 2
out
rt channel drone 5
wait 1
expect_out USB 80 34 00
expect_out USB 80 39 00
expect_out USB B0 7B 00
expect sounding0 0
wait 13400
expect tick 30850
expect sounding0 0
expect sounding5 2
tap PLAY
# the arranger's ending: Ambient drift's ambient plateau ends on bar 288 (tick 1105920, 960 s from tick 0); the
# transport stops there by itself once that tick is out (the drone's last off is on it: nothing left to flush)
rt load ambient
dumpmidi app/build/scenarios/stop_flush/ending.txt
tap PLAY
wait 959000
expect playing 1
wait 2000
expect playing 0
dumpis 1 FC 00 00
dumpis 2 F8 00 00
dumpcount 80 39 00 1105920
expect dumpcount 1
dumpcount FC 00 00 1105920
expect dumpcount 1
dumpcount B0 7B 00
expect dumpcount 0
expect sounding 0
expect queued 0
expect dumpbad 0
